# Bath brush 0: a long-handled bath brush lying on the floor (30 times life size), 12 m long (x), the wooden handle 0.9 m thick, the head 3.6 m long and 2.4 m wide (z) with its
# bristles standing up, 2.4 m tall in all (a wooden back 0.6 m, bristles on it). The handle end is at -x, the head at +x. Origin at the middle of its length on y = 0.
# Knee cover and wall: the handle is shot over and jumped, the head is a wall. Convex collider.
format 1
collider convex

Detail detail=0.5
    Union
        # The handle, rounded at the free end, lying on the floor; it runs into the head's back
        Material material=bath_wood
            Intersection
                SmoothUnion smoothness=0.2
                    Capsule a=(-5.55, 0.45, 0) b=(3.0, 0.45, 0) radius=0.45
                    # The head's wooden back, a flat rounded plate
                    Translate translation=(4.2, 0.3, 0)
                        RoundBox size=(1.8, 0.3, 1.2) roundness=0.2
                # The blend swells a little under the floor: cut it flat there
                Translate translation=(0, 1.5, 0)
                    Box size=(8, 1.5, 4)
        # The bristles: a dense block on the back, a little rounded on top
        Material material=bath_bristle
            Translate translation=(4.2, 1.5, 0)
                RoundBox size=(1.68, 0.9, 1.08) roundness=0.25
